    {
      "id": "d1462144-8768-4f2f-8354-c4e6cf68d8de",
      "name": "Sticky Note ba7a0f2a",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -464,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Save email invoices to Google Drive, sorted by month, with a monthly invoice sheet\n\nWatches Gmail for invoice emails, files every invoice in Google Drive under **Invoices folder \u2192 YYYY \u2192 YYYY-MM**, and logs it in a monthly Google Sheet. Missing folders and sheets are created automatically.\n\n### How it works\n1. **New invoice email** checks Gmail every 15 minutes for invoice emails not yet labelled `invoices-processed`.\n2. **Compute accounting month** works out the year and month folder names from the date the email arrived, and finds the invoice link in the email if there is one.\n3. Each email is handled one at a time: the year and month folders are found, or created if missing.\n4. **PDF attachments** are used as they are. **Invoices sent as a link** (Paddle, Stripe, ...) are downloaded, or rendered to a print-style PDF with PDF.co.\n5. **Claude** reads each invoice: supplier name, supplier VAT code, issue date, amount and currency.\n6. The PDF is saved as `YYYY-MM-DD - name.pdf` and a row is added to **Invoices YYYY-MM** in the month folder.\n7. The email gets the `invoices-processed` label so it is never filed twice.\n\n### Setup (about 10 minutes)\n1. Connect **Gmail**, **Google Drive**, **Google Sheets** and **Anthropic** credentials.\n2. In Gmail, create a label called `invoices-processed`, then pick it in **Label email as processed**.\n3. In **Settings**, paste the ID of your invoices folder (the part after `/folders/` in its Drive URL). Set `filePreviousMonth` to true if invoices received early in a month belong to the previous month.\n4. Adjust the Gmail search in **New invoice email** to match your suppliers.\n5. Optional: connect **PDF.co** for invoices that only arrive as a web link, and list allowed sites in `renderLinkDomains`.\n6. Test with an invoice email, then activate the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "337247ca-a273-48e9-b4a1-c23da98343c8",
      "name": "Sticky Note 7be82109",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        160,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### Settings\n- `invoicesFolderId`: your Google Drive invoices folder ID\n- `filePreviousMonth`: file invoices under the previous month\n- `renderLinkDomains`: optional, e.g. `paddle.com, stripe.com`. Empty = render invoice links from any site"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "577bb646-6396-41c8-b9e5-3d06848ac593",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1f487b96",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2896,
        608
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "### Invoices sent as a link\nMany providers (Paddle, Stripe, Lemon Squeezy, Shopify, ...) email a link instead of a PDF. The workflow picks the most likely invoice link in the email:\n- link returns a **PDF** \u2192 uploaded directly\n- link opens an **invoice web page** \u2192 rendered to a print-style PDF with **PDF.co** (needs a PDF.co API key; n8n Cloud may provide one through n8n credits)\n- link opens a **login page**, or its site is not in `renderLinkDomains` \u2192 skipped; the email is still labelled and the reason is shown in **Collect invoice files**"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
